id hybrix
name Hybrix
appeared 2025
creators Pete Gonzalez
tags pl
website https://www.hybrix.dev
description The programming language of Hybrix, a virtual computer with a 32-bit CPU called Chombit. It is small, imperative, statically typed, and garbage-collected, with classes and inheritance. Its design goal is that a programmer can understand any program all the way down to the machine: each variable has a fixed address for its lifetime, and every instruction has a documented cycle cost.
fileExtensions hyb
writtenIn typescript
compilesTo chombit

isOpenSource false
docs https://www.hybrix.dev/docs/compiler
rosettaCode https://rosettacode.org/wiki/Category:Hybrix
country United States
funFact https://github.com/writenrun/hybrix-framework/blob/main/assembly/gc.casm
 The garbage collector is less than 260 CPU instructions of hand-coded Chombit assembly.

example
 module main
   func start()
     # Minimal initialization of the Hybrix framework console
     console::init(io::tilemap_a)
     var font_layer: tile_layer
     font_layer <- new tile_layer(io::tilemap_a, io::tileset_a_addresses)
     font_layer.load_tileset(art::fonts[0])
 
     var i: int
     i <- 1
     loop
       # Print the number
       console::print_int(i)
       # Print a special "newline" character, starting a new line
       console::print("{n}")
 
       # When i reaches 10, drop out of the loop
       if i = 10
       do drop
 
       i <- i + 1
     end loop
   end func
 end module

